 [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4b31e2fa4a4f35568b00e90641bc6bb612608fe8671d9ca6052a21d4e7f446e8","event_uuid":"e9f06fe3-5c94-4f78-a538-f71af5df7abd","position":{"commit_sha":"990f97574f2fc4bdfaf5fff956ddaba539d2b4f8","position":"1786669592461454001-e9f06fe3-5c94-4f78-a538-f71af5df7abd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"82be5d0e255311900bbc9438f39bb1b5db46edbb9f37f92007684763e5e2c719","event_uuid":"3edc6b72-fab2-46be-b5c6-f55ffa4ab00e","position":{"commit_sha":"b3b710a420136b5730e7295b49696886eb9c9e69","position":"1786670501156207882-3edc6b72-fab2-46be-b5c6-f55ffa4ab00e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9f7892e7f3f124137d94cd813bc60d0ad29adfab8e9002fa3df0603a431f6ece","event_uuid":"11501f7e-aca8-4b46-8ca3-b0786578969d","position":{"commit_sha":"f57f647cbe7daf757617254b56f201488316fcd0","position":"1786673061305533170-11501f7e-aca8-4b46-8ca3-b0786578969d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Held-out TDD landed as Gerrit change 1754 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1754). Two ensure units (projects-seed, projects-compat-stamp) in new src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py; wired into ensures.py REGISTRY_IDS/_registry after store-compat; test_ensures.py freeze literal + docs/migrations.md updated. Behavioural oracle (8 tests) authored RED-first, implementer held out to happy-path only, full suite validated GREEN with mutation teeth. Awaiting Verified+1 before close.","timestamp":1786668298638400001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Amended (Change-Id Idde595c, Gerrit 1754) with Option-B fix: seed now fires only when the store has existing tickets (_store_has_tickets guard), so fresh stores keep an empty projects set and c927's bridge-projects contract stays green. Oracle 8/8, mutation teeth verified, lint/typecheck/complexity clean.","timestamp":1786669592461454001}],"created_at":1786160104184975001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"00ab3e96-4ced-4632-80bc-4340f2ebe8f5","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"c927-0a68-4465-42a2"},{"link_uuid":"cdf463ed-8d74-4430-aa86-3dab1daa76ba","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"67f9-4a07-9667-446a"},{"link_uuid":"4568fd4c-bcb6-4e80-a785-05cabd470e46","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ec5c-41d0-1d40-4b8b"},{"link_uuid":"3edc6b72-fab2-46be-b5c6-f55ffa4ab00e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0d65-3b4d-f47f-4b43"},{"link_uuid":"11501f7e-aca8-4b46-8ca3-b0786578969d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3e64-28ea-54f8-4c61"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nExisting stores — including client deployments — have no `.bridge_state/projects.json` and no\n`bridge_project` on any ticket. Without a migration they read every ticket as absent-project with no\nrecorded legacy default for the resolver to fall back to, so a store that syncs today stops syncing on\nupgrade.\n\n## Prerequisites (substrate, from cited deps — already `depends_on` edges)\n\n- `[rebar:c927-0a68-4465-42a2]` — the projects-mapping store `projects_store.py`: the\n  `.bridge_state/projects.json` record (`{version, legacy_default, projects}`), `load_mapping`, the\n  `Mapping` dataclass, the tri-state resolver `resolve_project` (absent field → `legacy_default`;\n  `\"\"` → `None`; key → verbatim), and `set_project`/`read_projects`.\n- `[rebar:67f9-4a07-9667-446a]` — registers `multi-project-bridge` in `KNOWN_CAPABILITIES`\n  (`src/rebar/_store/compat.py`), so\n  a store may stamp it and still pass its own compat gate.\n\n`Backend.project` (`_backend.py:598-605`, the effective write/create scope) is pre-existing.\n\n## Approach\n\nShip the migration as ensure units on the idempotent registry (`src/rebar/_store/ensures.py`,\n`REGISTRY_IDS` `:66`, `_registry()` `:82`) — rebar's sanctioned seam (`docs/migrations.md:40-56`; the\nordered School-A ledger is deliberately not built, `:14-16`). Units run at init/re-init,\n`fsck --repair`, and MCP boot (`:57-65`), so a client store converges with no operator action.\n\n**No ticket events.** An EDIT-per-ticket migration would be a four-figure event write under the store\nlock, and MCP-boot runs the sweep on a short lock budget and skips when contended (`:63-65`) — so it\nwould silently skip at one entry point and converge unpredictably. Instead the unit records\n`legacy_default` once, and `resolve_project` `[rebar:c927-0a68-4465-42a2]` treats every absent-field ticket as\nbelonging to it. One small write migrates the whole store.\n\nTwo units, both check-then-act and safe to re-run:\n\n1. **Seed the mapping.** If `.bridge_state/projects.json` `[rebar:c927-0a68-4465-42a2]` is absent, write it with\n   `legacy_default` and a single `projects` entry from `Backend.project` (`_backend.py:598-605`); if\n   present, return `ok` and write nothing. Tree-check the committed\n   `tickets:.bridge_state/projects.json` blob before committing so a converged store makes zero commits\n   (`docs/migrations.md:45-46`).\n2. **Converge the capability stamp (backstop, NOT the trigger).** Per the parent epic 0e68, the\n   *authoritative* `multi-project-bridge` stamp is written by the `bridge projects` set/remove write\n   path — the stamp and the mapping mutation land in the SAME tracker commit (one atomic publish). This\n   ensure unit is only a **convergence backstop for residual divergence**: when the mapping already\n   holds more than one project but `.store-compat.json`'s `required_capabilities` lacks\n   `multi-project-bridge` (a legacy store, or a crash between the write path's two writes), it adds the\n   token; a single-project store is never stamped and stays usable by older binaries. It is\n   level-triggered on the mapping state and decoupled from *how* the store became multi-project, and is\n   never the primary trigger — the seed above only ever makes a **one-project** mapping, so this unit\n   never fires from the same sweep's seed. The token is registered in `KNOWN_CAPABILITIES` by\n   prerequisite `[rebar:67f9-4a07-9667-446a]` (`src/rebar/_store/compat.py`, the `KNOWN_CAPABILITIES`\n   frozenset), so a stamped store still passes `check_store_compat` on this binary — this story makes\n   **no** `compat.py` edit, and a test asserts a two-project stamped store passes the gate.\n\nIds are new and never reused (`docs/migrations.md:50-51`).\n\n**Unit bodies live in a new `src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py`**, not `init.py` (where the six\nexisting units live, e.g. `_store_compat_unit` `:509`). `init.py` is **758 lines** — ~42 under the\n800-line gate (`.github/module-size-limit.txt`), so this is a **cohesion** choice, not size-forced:\nthe projects migration is distinct from init's `.gitignore`/`.gitattributes` constants. `ensures.py`\n(257 lines) gains only its two registry entries.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py` (new) — both unit bodies\n- `src/rebar/_store/ensures.py` — two `REGISTRY_IDS` entries + two `_registry()` mappings\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_ensures.py` — update the hardcoded `expected` id-set literal in\n  `test_registry_id_set_is_frozen` (`:57`, the six existing ids) to add the two new ids so the\n  registry-agreement test passes\n- `docs/migrations.md` — document the two units and the `multi-project-bridge` token's meaning for\n  other binaries/operators (it gates `.store-compat.json` compatibility)\n- `tests/integration/test_ensure_project_mapping.py` (new) — the behavioural oracle below\n\n## Testing\n\nReal temp git repos and refs (the shared standard's git row) — the units commit to `tickets` and the\nzero-commit-when-converged property is only observable against real refs.\n\n- Happy path: sweeping a no-mapping store creates one whose `legacy_default` equals the backend\n  project, and every ticket resolves to it via `resolve_project`.\n- Load-bearing: the sweep writes **zero ticket events** — assert the event-file set is identical before\n  and after (distinguishes this from an EDIT-per-ticket migration).\n- Idempotence: a second sweep returns `ok` for both units and the tickets-branch tip SHA is unchanged.\n- Conditional stamp (contrast pair): one-project → `required_capabilities` empty; two-project → exactly\n  `multi-project-bridge`. The one-project half proves the stamp is genuinely conditional.\n- Compat-gate safety: a two-project stamped store still passes `check_store_compat` on this binary.\n- Failure path: a raising unit is recorded `failed` and does not abort the sweep or caller.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A no-mapping store gains one whose `legacy_default` equals the configured backend project;\n      real-git test reads the seeded record.\n- [ ] Every absent-`bridge_project` ticket resolves to that default via `resolve_project`\n      `[rebar:c927-0a68-4465-42a2]`; same test.\n- [ ] The sweep writes zero ticket events; the event-file set is identical before and after.\n- [ ] A second sweep returns `ok` for both units.\n- [ ] A second sweep leaves the tickets-branch tip SHA unchanged (compared across two sweeps).\n- [ ] A one-project mapping leaves `required_capabilities` empty; real-git test.\n- [ ] A two-project mapping adds exactly `multi-project-bridge`; real-git test.\n- [ ] A two-project stamped store still passes `check_store_compat` on this binary; test invokes the\n      gate.\n- [ ] The two new ids are added to `REGISTRY_IDS`.\n- [ ] The two new ids are mapped in `_registry()`.\n- [ ] The two new ids are added to the `expected` literal in `test_registry_id_set_is_frozen`\n      (`test_ensures.py:57`) so that test passes.\n- [ ] A raising unit is recorded `failed` and does not abort the sweep or caller; test monkeypatches a\n      raising unit into `_registry()`.\n- [ ] `docs/migrations.md` documents the two ensure units and the `multi-project-bridge` token's\n      compat meaning for other binaries/operators (that it gates `.store-compat.json` compatibility).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py","reason":"new module holding both ensure unit bodies (seed-mapping + conditional capability stamp)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/ensures.py","reason":"register the two new unit ids in REGISTRY_IDS and map them in _registry()"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_ensures.py","reason":"update the hardcoded expected id-set literal in test_registry_id_set_is_frozen to include the two new units"},{"path":"docs/migrations.md","reason":"document the two new units and the multi-project-bridge capability token meaning"},{"path":"tests/integration/test_ensure_project_mapping.py","reason":"behavioural oracle: zero-event migration, idempotent second sweep, conditional stamp, compat-gate safety"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","67f9-4a07-9667-446a"],["depends_on","c927-0a68-4465-42a2"],["parent","0e68-41eb-5782-4336"],["relates_to","0d65-3b4d-f47f-4b43"],["relates_to","3e64-28ea-54f8-4c61"],["relates_to","ec5c-41d0-1d40-4b8b"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","parent_status_uuid":"9ec86fc8-7f8c-4bb4-8b93-56e0936bbee8","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"462d-8d84-122a-4812","ticket_type":"story","title":"Legacy-store migration: ensure units seeding the project mapping without writing ticket events","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c8b83c65-25a6-4cf7-b712-6b367426dada","dad2f9da-1e3b-4fd7-9fd0-db35f04240aa","c66144a8-383c-4295-bc29-8cd31a9baeaa","d1a66fba-c79b-45f5-859a-a245c1fe50eb","1f29e97e-d5bb-423e-88ba-06e2a43f509b","a64af345-e181-49a2-95d5-5d56ca6b775d","048d1295-532e-4692-827a-94a1bbecb19d","01545806-d64f-4a11-8588-b6e1f1ac4962","b58ee37f-ebcb-4c37-a5a8-79ad53ddb557","9ec86fc8-7f8c-4bb4-8b93-56e0936bbee8","f7379159-5cbf-49d2-bd8c-c5c0861d9146","da14f24b-dd09-46d5-8b6b-3c1b5e8b2a8b","4568fd4c-bcb6-4e80-a785-05cabd470e46","e9f06fe3-5c94-4f78-a538-f71af5df7abd","3edc6b72-fab2-46be-b5c6-f55ffa4ab00e","11501f7e-aca8-4b46-8ca3-b0786578969d"]},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786673061305533171,"uuid":"56b6e407-51d1-4ce4-bd3a-3eae7a66c50a"}